  ("where α and β, possibly empty, denote the rest formulas in a sequent." 0.1812 0.7675 0.3726 0.3860 0.3860 0.0134 0.00637 0.2710 0.0489 "CQDOTO+CMR12" 0.0151 nil nil 12)
  ("In natural deduction, a sequent is deduced from a set of axioms by applying" 0.2282 0.8730 0.3922 0.4056 0.4056 0.0134 0.00684 0.2493 0.0175 "CQDOTO+CMR12" 0.0151 nil nil 13)
  ("inference rules repeatedly. Each sequent is inferred from other sequents on earlier" 0.1812 0.8730 0.4119 0.4253 0.4253 0.0134 0.00709 0.2266 0.0738 "CQDOTO+CMR12" 0.0151 nil nil 11)
  ("lines in a proof according to inference rules, giving a better approximation to the" 0.1812 0.8731 0.4315 0.4449 0.4449 0.0134 0.00729 0.2302 0.0373 "CQDOTO+CMR12" 0.0151 nil nil 13)
  ("style of proofs used by mathematicians than Hilbert systems." 0.1812 0.6942 0.4511 0.4645 0.4645 0.0134 0.00637 0.2933 0.0384 "CQDOTO+CMR12" 0.0151 nil nil 8)
