  ("Proposition 3.2.10. The deductive system G is sound, i.e., if A ⊢_{G} B, then A ​|= B." 0.1812 0.8729 0.6390 0.6553 0.6540 0.0134 0.00529 0.3637 0.1115 "FSDBRE+CMBX12" 0.0151 t nil 16)
  ("Proof. It is easy to check that every inference rule of G is sound. In particular," 0.1812 0.8730 0.6712 0.6863 0.6863 0.0134 0.0083 0.2112 0.0513 "CQDOTO+CMR12" 0.0151 nil nil 15)
  ("the rules of operator introduction preserve the logical equivalence. In the rules of" 0.1812 0.8730 0.6924 0.7058 0.7058 0.0134 0.00719 0.2018 0.0266 "CQDOTO+CMR12" 0.0151 nil nil 12)
  ("operator elimination, some sequents generate two results. For example, (A ∧B ​| α)" 0.1812 0.8729 0.7104 0.7255 0.7255 0.0134 0.00592 0.3228 0.0707 "CQDOTO+CMR12" 0.0151 nil nil 12)
  ("infers both (a) (A ​| α) and (b) (B ​| α). If we bind the two results together by ∧," 0.1812 0.8729 0.7300 0.7451 0.7451 0.0134 0.00717 0.2524 0.0453 "CQDOTO+CMR12" 0.0151 nil nil 19)
  ("these rules preserve the logical equivalence, too. On the other hand, the cut rule" 0.1812 0.8730 0.7512 0.7647 0.7647 0.0134 0.00748 0.2137 0.0426 "CQDOTO+CMR12" 0.0151 nil nil 13)
  ("and the thinning rule do not preserve the logical equivalence; only the entailment" 0.1812 0.8730 0.7709 0.7843 0.7843 0.0134 0.00717 0.2293 0.0308 "CQDOTO+CMR12" 0.0151 nil nil 12)
  ("relation holds. That is, for the cut rule, (A ​| α), (¬A ​| β) ⊢(α ​| β), we have" 0.1812 0.8250 0.7889 0.8040 0.8040 0.0134 0.00637 0.3782 0.0638 "CQDOTO+CMR12" 0.0151 nil nil 18)
  ("(A ∨α) ∧(¬A ∨β) ​|= α ∨β," 0.4071 0.6470 0.8236 0.8387 0.8387 0.0151 0.00446 0.4839 0.0218 "TTNUXI+CMMI12" 0.0151 nil t 6)
  ("and for the thinning rule, (α) ⊢(A ​| α), we have α ​|= A ∨α." 0.1812 0.6989 0.8583 0.8734 0.8734 0.0134 0.00637 0.4088 0.0308 "CQDOTO+CMR12" 0.0151 nil nil 14)
